<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n8587" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνεω</span></b> , Adv.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>without a sound, in silence,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δὴν δ᾽ ἄ. ἦσαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					9.30
				</span></i>
			,<i><span class="en">
				695
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τίπτ᾽ ἄ. ἐγένεσθε;</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					2.323
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ δ᾽ ἄ. ἐγένοντο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					3.84
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				7.144
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				10.71
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἅπαντες ἧσθ᾽ ἄ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					2.240
				</span></i>
			.—In all the places cited it is joined with a pl.
			Verb, and is commonly written <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνεψ</span>
			(as if nom. pl. from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνεως</span>).</div>
